  "findings": [
    "ComponentRoseSelfArrow#drawRightSide applies lifecycle Area.deltaX1, subtracts1 from x2 for ASYNC only when drawing the bottom stroke, then restores1 for the head. The new special-return-tip branch applies this in that order, including thin half-heads. The first eight full-CLI depth/label/order/engine controls and the legacy right-directed half-head controls pass.",
    "Focused direction/depth/both-lifecycle controls disprove the shared model dependency: checker_focus_e0_r1_d0 is213px wide in Java versus170px in Rust. MessageSelfArrow#getStartingX has a reverse branch that subtracts preferred width and Step1Message reserves ConstraintBefore. SequenceSelfArrow::new has no direction argument and always returns right+activation_delta; the extent map and right-note shifts reuse it. The separate left painter cannot repair its missing left constraint.",
    "Six focused Teoz controls also fail (both lifecycle flags or attached half-head notes). The exact right-side ASYNC subtraction is supported, but its required live-envelope/component dependencies are not independently accepted. This verdict does not claim the one-unit subtraction itself is wrong.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
